`--help` is the discovery surface: it lists every verb of the I/O contract and the global flags
each of them accepts. Help text is asserted loosely — the verb names and flag names are the
contract, their descriptions are not.

-- cmd --
booping-tracker --help
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
usage: booping-tracker [-h] [--driver DRIVER] [--config-file CONFIG_FILE]
[..][--output {text,json}] [--dry-run]
[..]<verb> ...

booping tracker CLI

positional arguments:
  <verb>
    states[..]
    show[..]
    comment[..]
    issue-create[..]
    issue-update[..]
    relate[..]
    sync[..]

options:
  -h, --help[..]
  --driver DRIVER[..]
  --config-file CONFIG_FILE
[..]
[..]
  --output {text,json}[..]
  --dry-run[..]
-- stderr --
